      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "Habitats",
          "lines": [
            "Any terrain",
            "Forest, rocky areas, and underground"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Appearance",
          "lines": [
            "A long, segmented centipede with chitinous backplates. Forest specimens are brown or red, those in rocky areas are gray, and underground specimens are black."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Combat mechanics",
          "lines": [
            "Paralytic bite · The bite inflicts no direct damage. The victim saves vs. poison with a +4 bonus. On a failed save it is paralyzed for 2d6 hours. The Giant Centipede takes a −1 penalty to all its own saving throws.",
            "Camouflaged ambush · It relies on coloration to hide, drops from above or emerges from cover, and fights independently even when several are present."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Table notes",
          "lines": [
            "2–24 appearing. Common. No intelligence (0). Unsteady (5–7) morale. Active at any time, carnivorous, and neutral. No special defenses or magic resistance.",
            "Organization and treasure are Nil. The Hit Dice field gives 2 HP. The size field gives 1 ft. The prose says over 1 ft.",
            "Monstrous Manual, TSR 2140, January 1994 third printing, p. 42."
          ]
        }
      ],
