      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "Habitats",
          "lines": [
            "Any terrain",
            "Forest, rocky areas, and underground"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Appearance",
          "lines": [
            "A six-inch, many-legged centipede with chitinous body segments. It shares the Giant Centipede’s camouflage, including rocky gray and underground black specimens."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Combat mechanics",
          "lines": [
            "Paralytic bite · The bite inflicts no direct damage. A victim that fails its save vs. poison is immobilized for 1d6 hours. The prose treats this form as the Giant Centipede with exceptions, so the victim’s +4 save bonus carries over by reference.",
            "Own saving throws · The Huge Centipede takes a −2 penalty to its own saving throws."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Table notes",
          "lines": [
            "5–30 appearing. Common. No intelligence (0). Unsteady (5–7) morale. Active at any time, carnivorous, and neutral. No special defenses or magic resistance.",
            "Organization and treasure are Nil. The Hit Dice field gives 1 HP. Despite its title, this form is smaller than the Giant Centipede.",
            "Monstrous Manual, TSR 2140, January 1994 third printing, p. 42."
          ]
        }
      ],
