          "title": "Habitats",
          "lines": [
            "Any terrain",
            "Wilderness where it hunts deer-sized prey, and subterranean areas"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Appearance",
          "lines": [
            "A five-foot centipede with a long, segmented body and chitinous armor."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Combat mechanics",
          "lines": [
            "Acidic bite · The table gives 1–3 bite damage. The poison save receives no bonus. Failure means death. On a successful save, the acid deals 2d4 damage.",
            "Own saving throws · The Megalo-centipede has no penalty to its own saving throws."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Behavior mechanics",
          "lines": [
            "Solitary hunter · It stalks larger animals in the wilderness and humanoid-sized or smaller prey underground. Individuals do not hunt together."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Table notes",
          "lines": [
            "1–4 appearing. Very rare. Animal intelligence (1). Average (8–10) morale. Active at any time, carnivorous, and neutral. No special defenses or magic resistance.",
            "Organization and treasure are Nil.",
            "Monstrous Manual, TSR 2140, January 1994 third printing, p. 42."
          ]
        }
      ],
