      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "Habitats",
          "lines": [
            "Subterranean areas, hidden burrows, and lairs"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Appearance",
          "lines": [
            "A burrowing relative of the giant centipede at least 25 feet long, with powerful mandibles."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Combat mechanics",
          "lines": [
            "Burrow lunge · A lunge from its hidden burrow gets +2 to hit. A hit seizes the target in its mandibles. The lunge causes no damage until it chews through the armor.",
            "Armor breach · Leather or worse takes one round. Armor tougher than leather through chain mail takes two. Armor tougher than chain mail takes three. Once the armor is breached, the worm deals 2d8 damage automatically each round.",
            "Retreat · It releases the victim and retreats to its lair after taking at least 15 points of fire damage or losing 60% of its HP."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Lair mechanics",
          "lines": [
            "Carrion and treasure · It eats carrion, lays eggs in it, and may leave treasure from former victims in its lair."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Appearance notes mechanics",
          "lines": [
            "Body plan · The segmented body and short walking legs depict its stated kinship with centipedes. The book does not specify a palette for this form."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Table notes",
          "lines": [
            "1–6 appearing. Rare. No intelligence (0). Steady (12) morale. Active at any time, carnivorous, and neutral. No special defenses or magic resistance.",
            "Swarm organization. Treasure (M, N, Q). The attack table gives 2–8. The lunge text instead specifies automatic 2d8 per round after breaching armor.",
            "Monstrous Manual, TSR 2140, January 1994 third printing, p. 42."
          ]
        }
      ],
